# Missione multi-hop — BANCO DI CONTROLLO (held-out), scritto DOPO l'8/8 del banco della classe
# e SENZA toccare il ciclo (docs/plans/multi-hop-deep-memory.md §7.0, criterio 3 e 4).
# Problemi nuovi della stessa classe; per ognuno si e' verificato soltanto dove sono scritti
# gli anelli nei lead veri (tests/fixtures/wiki/SOURCES.tsv, search.tsv: risultati veri della
# ricerca di Wikipedia, 14 settembre 2026). Serve a misurare se l'8/8 e' generalita' o
# adattamento al banco.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

# H1 — monumento → paese (letto) → valuta (nota in KB: currency_of_country)
[test H1 a monument, the country read from its page, the currency known]
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> look things up yourself
> What currency is used in the country where the Taj Mahal stands?
<~ rupee
<! mysterious

# H2 — opera → compositore (letto) → nazionalita' (letta, modificatore della classe)
[test H2 an opera, its composer, his nationality]
!reset
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> look things up yourself
> What was the nationality of the composer of the opera Carmen?
<~ French
<! Spanish

# H3 — capitale → paese (whose) → lingua (nota in KB)
[test H3 whose capital, then a known language]
!reset
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> look things up yourself
> Which language is spoken in the country whose capital is Lima?
<~ Spanish

# H4 — descrizione → montagna (ricerca) → catena (letta), SENZA parola ponte nel prompt
[test H4 a description without a bridge word]
!reset
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> look things up yourself
> Which mountain range contains the highest mountain in Europe?
<~ Caucasus

# H6 — H2 a passi imperativi
[test H6 the chain of H2 given as steps]
!reset
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> look things up yourself
> Start from the opera Carmen. Identify its composer. Then determine his nationality.
<~ French

# C2 — CONTROLLO: il lead del Cairo non nomina il Nilo (sta nel corpo). Non si inventa.
[test C2 the river of Cairo is not in its lead, and is not invented]
!reset
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> look things up yourself
> Into which sea does the river that flows through the capital of Egypt empty?
<! Mediterranean
<! mysterious

# H5 — H1 in italiano (in fondo: la lingua resta appiccicosa, reperto del piano)
[test H5 the same as H1 in Italian]
!set PARROT0_LANG=it
!reset
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> cerca da solo
> Quale moneta si usa nel paese dove si trova il Taj Mahal?
<~ rupia
